<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
===============================================================================
Spartrak — category page composition (Figma 488:10810).

Figma's category page is four bands, in this order:

    488:18402   breadcrumbs                  (Magento's own, already correct)
    488:12966   HERO           full bleed    << added here
    507:5234    "تسوق بالمنتجات" tile rail    << added here
    488:12196   Explore: sidebar + grid      (already built, untouched)

and NOTHING else. There is no page title above the hero, no category image
band, no separate description block. So this file does two things: it mounts
the two new blocks, and it takes out the four blocks that would otherwise
render the same content a second time.

WHY THIS IS A THEME FILE AND NOT A MODULE ONE
===============================================================================
Two of the four removals below target blocks that Smartwave/porto's own
catalog_category_view.xml declares. Layout merges module files first and theme
files last, so the removals are only unambiguously the final word from here.
Spartrak/spartrak_rtl is a child of this theme, so it inherits the whole file.

The BLOCKS themselves live in Spartrak_Catalog, not in the theme, because they
are application behaviour rather than presentation — the same split the PDP
related rail already uses.

WHAT IS REMOVED, AND WHY EACH ONE
===============================================================================
  page.main.title            Magento's h1.page-title, which prints the
                             category name. Figma has no page title above the
                             hero, and the hero already renders the category's
                             headline as the page's h1. Two headings naming
                             the same category is neither the design nor good
                             document structure. The hero falls back to the
                             category name when no headline override is set,
                             so the h1 is never lost.

  category.image             Porto moves Magento's category-image block into
                             `content`. The category `image` attribute is what
                             this page's own tile rail uses as each CHILD
                             category's thumbnail, so admins will be filling
                             it in — and left mounted, the current category's
                             thumbnail would also print full width above the
                             product grid, which is in no frame of the design.

  category.description.default
  category_desc_main_column  Both print the category description. The hero now
                             owns it (see Block\Category\Hero for why the hero
                             reuses `description` instead of adding a second
                             field), so these would each print it again.

  category_banner            Porto's own category-description banner in
                             page.top. Same content, same reason. This is the
                             component the Spartrak hero REPLACES, which under
                             CLAUDE.md section 2 makes the Spartrak
                             implementation the source of truth for it.

  category_leftnav           Porto's `.block-category-list` — a plain ordered
                             list of the current category's CHILDREN, which
                             its own template then relocates above the filter
                             sidebar with an inline jQuery snippet. That is
                             the exact job the Spartrak tile rail now does,
                             from the same data, so leaving it mounted showed
                             every child twice: once as a tile and once as a
                             bare link list. Removing the block also removes
                             that inline script and the DOM move it performs
                             on every category page.

                             Declared by Porto in
                             Mageplaza_LayeredNavigation/layout/
                             catalog_category_view_type_layered.xml, which is
                             a `_type_layered` handle — so the removal below
                             is repeated in this theme's own copy of that
                             handle. A block added on a handle can only be
                             removed on a handle that is also loaded.

`category.cms` is deliberately LEFT ALONE. It renders whatever CMS block an
admin picked in "Add CMS Block" on the category — genuinely separate content
that this page does not otherwise show, and nothing in Figma contradicts it.

The mobile filter drawer is NOT wired from here any more. It used to be a
data-mage-init attribute on <body>, duplicated in the search layout, and the
button did nothing whenever that chain broke. The behaviour now ships on the
button itself in Magento_Catalog/templates/product/list/toolbar.phtml, which
both this route and search render, so neither layout file needs to know the
module name. Do not add it back here.
-->
<page xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="urn:magento:framework:View/Layout/etc/page_configuration.xsd">
    <body>
        <referenceContainer name="columns.top">
            <!--
              columns.top sits inside .page-main and before .columns, which is
              exactly where both bands go: below the breadcrumbs (those are a
              child of .page-wrapper, outside .page-main) and above the
              sidebar + grid. Both bands escape .page-main's 48px gutter in
              CSS, from the same LESS variable that sets it — see
              web/css/source/components/_category-top.less.
            -->
            <block class="Spartrak\Catalog\Block\Category\Hero"
                   name="spartrak.category.hero"
                   template="Spartrak_Catalog::category/hero.phtml"
                   before="-">
                <arguments>
                    <!--
                      The hero deliberately declares no constructor (see the
                      block), so its one collaborator is handed in here. Same
                      resolver the rail injects directly, so a category image
                      URL is built one way on this page.
                    -->
                    <argument name="image_resolver" xsi:type="object">Spartrak\Catalog\ViewModel\CategoryImage</argument>
                </arguments>
            </block>

            <block class="Spartrak\Catalog\Block\Category\Rail"
                   name="spartrak.category.rail"
                   template="Spartrak_Catalog::category/rail.phtml"
                   after="spartrak.category.hero"/>

            <!--
              The SECOND admin-managed banner, directly below the rail.

              Not a Figma component - 488:10810 has nothing between the rail
              and the product area - so it is built in the hero's own language
              rather than as a new treatment. See Block\Category\Promo.

              Same image_resolver instance as the hero, so a category image
              URL is built exactly one way on this page.
            -->
            <block class="Spartrak\Catalog\Block\Category\Promo"
                   name="spartrak.category.promo"
                   template="Spartrak_Catalog::category/promo.phtml"
                   after="spartrak.category.rail">
                <arguments>
                    <argument name="image_resolver" xsi:type="object">Spartrak\Catalog\ViewModel\CategoryImage</argument>
                </arguments>

                <!--
                  THE QUICK-SEARCH DIALOG — the same cascading finder the
                  homepage renders, in the modal shell Figma 573:22900 draws.

                  This mounted Spartrak_Homepage's own CascadeSearch block at
                  first, with no section. It rendered NOTHING: AbstractSection
                  ::_toHtml() returns '' when getSection() is null, so the
                  dialog was empty and the button — which promo.phtml only
                  draws when the dialog produced markup — disappeared with it.

                  Block\Category\QuickSearch replaces it. What is shared is the
                  part that matters: both read the same
                  Spartrak\Homepage\ViewModel\CascadeOptions, which is also
                  what the AJAX endpoint calls, and the dialog runs the same
                  spartrakCascadeSearch widget over the same data-finder-*
                  contract. Only the section machinery — which was never this
                  dialog's to use — is not shared.

                  Declared as a CHILD of the promo block so the button and the
                  dialog cannot get out of step: promo.phtml emits the button
                  only when getChildHtml() returned markup, so a finder with
                  nothing to offer leaves no orphan control on the banner.
                -->
                <block class="Spartrak\Catalog\Block\Category\QuickSearch"
                       name="spartrak.category.promo.quick_search"
                       as="quick_search"
                       template="Spartrak_Catalog::category/quick-search.phtml"/>
            </block>
        </referenceContainer>

        <referenceBlock name="page.main.title" remove="true"/>
        <referenceBlock name="category.image" remove="true"/>
        <referenceBlock name="category.description.default" remove="true"/>
        <referenceBlock name="category_desc_main_column" remove="true"/>
        <referenceBlock name="category_banner" remove="true"/>
    </body>
</page>
